==To Start==
Speak with [[Dorn Geargrinder]] located in [[Rumble Ridge]], [[Sunstone Valley]].
==Goals==
Help Dorn Geargrinder by regrouping the Freewheelers.
*Talk to Golmie Greasebeard
*Talk to Headmaster Merk
*Talk to Freewheelers - /3
*Return to Dorn Geargrinder
==Steps==
#Speak with [[Dorn Geargrinder]] located in [[Rumble Ridge]], [[Sunstone Valley]].
#*"It seems that while we was in Shrouded Glade, this gang called the <font color='#D9781A'>Skullz</font> took over <font color='#D9781A'>Rumble Ridge</font>. And now most of the <font color='#D9781A'>Freewheelers</font> have deserted! If only Gus was here..." -Dorn Geargrinder
#Speak with [[Golmie Greasebeard]] located in [[Rumble Ridge]], [[Sunstone Valley]].
#*"Dorn's havin' a hard time acceptin' the loss of his brother Gus. He's a blasted hero and the only one that can pull the gang back together." -Golmie Greasebeard
#Speak with [[Headmaster Merk]] located in [[Rumble Ridge]], [[Sunstone Valley]].
#*"Dorn needs to be reminded of the trust his brother Gus had in him. Gus knew Dorn was a natural leader. If you can find the other Freewheelers and tell them of Dorn’s accomplishments in Shrouded Glade, I am certain they would follow him." -Headmaster Merk
#Speak with [[Freewheelers]] located in [[Rumble Ridge]], [[Sunstone Valley]].
##One [[Freewheeler]] is located between [[Wheelie Pete's Roadhouse]] and [[The Rumbledome]] in [[Rumble Ridge]], [[Sunstone Valley]].
##*"A lot's gone wrong for the Freewheelers recently. Why should we follow Dorn?" -Freewheeler
##*"Dorn's a good leader!" -Player response
##One [[Freewheeler]] is located near the [[Sandscale Oasis]] entrance in [[Sunstone Valley]].
##*"Dorn proved to be a good leader when we took the bridge site, we should probably follow him now." -Freewheeler
##*"Hurry Up!" -Player response
##One [[Freewheeler]] is located near the [[Rough Rider Raceway]] in [[Sunstone Valley]].
##*"Can Dorn really expect to fill his brother’s shoes?" -Freewheeler
##*"Dorn was born to lead." -Player response
#Speak with [[Dorn Geargrinder]] located in [[Rumble Ridge]], [[Sunstone Valley]].
#*"Thanks <Player Name>. Gus never doubted me and I guess I shouldn’t either. Leading the Freewheelers to glory is the best way I can honor his memory." -Dorn Geargrinder
